# Only the energy tolerance needs overriding; force/stress/fatal use the
# global defaults (1e-4 / 1e-3 / 1).
#
# This deliberately-minimal metallic EXX+SOC case (ecutwfc=5, anisotropic
# 2x2x1 k-mesh, EXX updated every step) never reaches a stable SCF fixed
# point and stops mid-oscillation, so the endpoint is sensitive to tiny
# numerical seeds. np=1 is bit-identical run-to-run; under MPI the EXX/LibRI
# reduction order shifts the final energy by up to ~9e-7 eV at np=4
# (measured, three repeats against the np=1 reference). Stress stays within
# 2.1e-4 and the force is exactly zero by symmetry. The discrete
# symmetry/magnetic-group assertions (O_h / C_4h / nksibz=3), the real
# purpose of this test, remain exact.
#
# The reference was regenerated after merging upstream PR #8017, which
# applies LibXC vrho down to 1e-10 (QE convention): the shifted vxc seed
# moves this non-converged trajectory to a different endpoint (~0.11 eV),
# while converged HSE cases shift only by ~1e-5 eV.
threshold 0.00001
